# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — ProcessQueue parity closure slice
# Recorded: 2026-10-22 23:15:00 UTC
# Code revision: aa3cec73

## Compatibility finding and change

Pinned Java 5.5.1 `ProcessQueue.removeMessage` mutates only the ready
`msgTreeMap`. A message returned by `takeMessages` is held in the separate
orderly in-flight map, so removal by offset must leave its count/size intact
for a later `commit`. Java also leaves `consuming` unchanged when the final
ready message is removed. Rust now follows both flows while preserving its
internal batch ownership.

The invoked Java `ConsumerFacadeApiFixtures` comparison adds `removeInFlight`
and `dispatchAfterRemove` cases. Updated fixture SHA-256:
`67aac16425d8ac98e2d2cde4ff53a91e68b080b429711852979eb302d173dc5e`.
The focused regressions are
`remove_message_matches_java_for_in_flight_entries` and
`remove_message_preserves_dispatch_state_until_empty_take`.

